                    "name": "explanation",
                    "offset": {
                      "lg": 0
                    },
                    "span": {
                      "lg": 1
                    },
                    "content": {
                      "text": [
                        {
                          "locale": "en",
                          "text": "This model shows validation errors on Custom Screen Elements, which projects report themselves instead of letting the Form Engine compute them.\n<br/>\n\"Create custom errors\" raises one error on a field and one on each Custom Screen Element, including the one inside the detached repeat on screen 3. They all appear in the same validation bar, and \"Go to Issue\" jumps to the custom element - which works because the devapp renders the <code>uiId</code> the Form Engine passes to it.\n<br/>\nControl2 carries a real validation rule (3 to 6 characters), so you can see a computed error next to the custom ones. On screen 3 you can move, copy and delete repeat rows to watch the custom errors follow their row or disappear with it.\n<br/>\nThe navigation buttons show how validation interacts with them: leaving a screen without validation or with a partial one keeps the custom errors, a full validation clears them."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
